-- title:
--   Strict transforms have Igusa curves as geometric fibres
-- statement:
--   Fix $N_0\ge 1$ and a prime $q$ with $q\nmid N_0$, and let $\mathfrak X$ be a Deligne–Rapoport model package [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel N₀ q hqN`](def/ModularCurve_DRModelPackageLevel.html#L71) for level $N_0q$ over $R=$ [`ModularCurve.DRLevel.R q`](def/ModularCurve_DRModelPackageLevel.html#L32) (the localisation of $\mathbb Q$'s rational integers at $q$ used throughout). Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain with a ring map $\rho_O\colon R\to O$ whose maximal ideal is generated by the image of $q$, let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $q$ and $t\colon O\to\kappa$ a ring map. Assume [`V3AsmLevel.SiteHyps`](def/ModularCurve_ResolvedModelSiteLevel.html#L270), i.e. the node set of the level site is finite, oriented crossing charts exist, the étale-neighbourhood datum `EtNbhd` holds, the map sending a node to its point of $\mathfrak X_O$ is injective with closed image points, and the model hypotheses `ModelHyps q O` hold; assume also that both points $\xi_j$ ($j\in\{0,1\}$) lie in the open locus `X0` of the chart input, the complement of the finitely many node points. Let $Y\to\mathfrak X_O$ be the glued resolution [`V3AsmLevel.toDR`](def/ModularCurve_ResolvedModelSiteLevel.html#L289), with structure map [`V3AsmLevel.toBase`](def/ModularCurve_ResolvedModelSiteLevel.html#L290) $=$ `toDR` followed by $\mathfrak X_O\to\operatorname{Spec}O$, and for $i\in\{0,1\}$ let $C_i\hookrightarrow Y$ be the closed subscheme attached to the ideal-sheaf datum [`V3AsmLevel.comp … (Sum.inl i)`](def/ModularCurve_ResolvedModelSiteLevel.html#L410). Then for each $i$ there is a morphism $e$ from the fibre product of $C_i\to Y\to\operatorname{Spec}O$ with $\operatorname{Spec}\kappa\to\operatorname{Spec}O$ to [`ModularCurve.DRLevel.fibre0 (t\circ\rho_O)`](def/ModularCurve_DRModelPackageLevel.html#L45), the base change to $\kappa$ of the level-$N_0$ Igusa scheme, such that $e$ is an isomorphism, $e$ commutes with the two projections to $\operatorname{Spec}\kappa$, and $e$ followed by the $i$-th component $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{comp}$ of the geometric fibre and by the base-change map `DRLevel.bcMap ρO toκ` equals the projection $C_i\times_O\kappa\to C_i$ followed by $C_i\hookrightarrow Y$ and [`V3AsmLevel.toDR`](def/ModularCurve_ResolvedModelSiteLevel.html#L289).
--
--   This identifies the two strict transforms in the resolved Deligne–Rapoport model of $X_0(N_0q)$ over $O$: after base change to $\kappa$ each is, compatibly with the maps into $\mathfrak X_O$, the level-$N_0$ Igusa curve over $\kappa$, as in the classical description of the special fibre of $X_0(N_0q)$ at $q$. It supplies the `strict_iso` datum used by [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.exists_dRResolvedModelPackageLevel_and_dRResolvedModelChartsLevelRam`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.exists_dRResolvedModelPackageLevel_and_dRResolvedModelChartsLevelRam) in the construction of the resolved model package.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_V3AsmLevel_strict_iso.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_ResolvedModelSiteLevel

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

set_option autoImplicit false

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits AlgebraicGeometry

attribute [local instance] ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.neZero_mul

theorem V3AsmLevel.strict_iso
    (N₀ q : ℕ) [NeZero N₀] [Fact q.Prime] (hqN : ¬ q ∣ N₀) (𝔛 : ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel N₀ q hqN)
    (O : Type) [CommRing O] [IsDomain O] [IsDiscreteValuationRing O] (ρO : ModularCurve.DRLevel.R q →+* O)
    (hϖ : IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal O = Ideal.span {((q : ℕ) : O)})
    (κ : Type) [Field κ] [CharP κ q] [IsAlgClosed κ] [DecidableEq κ] (toκ : O →+* κ)
    (H : V3AsmLevel.SiteHyps 𝔛 O ρO κ toκ) (hξ : ∀ j, V3AsmLevel.ξ 𝔛 O ρO κ toκ j ∈ (V3AsmLevel.C 𝔛 O ρO κ toκ hϖ H).X0)
    (i : Fin 2) :
    ∃ e : pullback ((V3AsmLevel.comp 𝔛 O ρO κ toκ hϖ H hξ (Sum.inl i)).subschemeι ≫ V3AsmLevel.toBase 𝔛 O ρO κ toκ hϖ H)
        (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom toκ)) ⟶ ModularCurve.DRLevel.fibre0 (N₀ := N₀) (toκ.comp ρO),
      IsIso e ∧ e ≫ pullback.snd _ _ = pullback.snd _ _ ∧
        e ≫ 𝔛.comp κ (toκ.comp ρO) i ≫ ModularCurve.DRLevel.bcMap ρO toκ =
          pullback.fst _ _ ≫ (V3AsmLevel.comp 𝔛 O ρO κ toκ hϖ H hξ (Sum.inl i)).subschemeι ≫ V3AsmLevel.toDR 𝔛 O ρO κ toκ hϖ H := by sorry
